!! The blur, named

# ''`writable-bag` vs the mount's default'' — DISSOLVED. The record designates `wikis/{slug}/working`; `defaultWritableSlot` names that slot, and the mounted working layer receives default writes.
# ''Two draft documents wear one slot name'' — DISSOLVED. THE ONE slot-doc resolver (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/slot-doc-resolver.ts`, the law `resolveSlotDoc` in `@lararium/mesh`): the PersonaGroup × fingerprint binding WHEN the vessel holds a seated PersonaGroup cap, ELSE the device floor `wikis/{slug}/drafts/{did}` — and the record says which (`face-reach`). Every site reads through it: the island's slot grants, the host mount (by the daemon proxy), `wiki init`, `prune-stale`, `put recipe=<slug>`, `where`, the ACTION verbs. Weld witness: `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/slot-doc-resolver.test.ts` S3 (five sites, one doc, seated and unseated). ⚠ THE MOUNT'S TRACE IS THE TRACE: a wiki the vessel mounted this session fingerprinted the canon doc it holds; a verb re-deriving the url from a registry pointer read a DIFFERENT doc when a peer's founding rewrote the shared oracle plane's `bags/lares` pointer mid-session (measured in the two-vessel e2e) — the resolver keeps the mount's trace per slug and reuses it.
# ''Per-DID or per-PersonaGroup'' — RULED: both, by seat. Fleet when a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap stands; the DID floor when not — a private device so far. A seat landing later resolves the face doc from then on; the floor stays the device's own (no migration).
# ''What "volatile / per-device" holds: temp ALONE.'' Presence stands unbuilt — no `presence` slot, no `$:/status/` beyond what TW5 writes; `$:/status/*` and `$:/boot/*` and most `$:/state/*` route to temp (`lar-bag-paths.tid:8-10`, `:15`). `personal` syncs across the face's own devices by design (its view state and what it keeps for itself), so the ruling's "all here don't [sync]" holds for temp and not for personal. Per-device state that MUST survive a reboot (a device's own window layout, a local-only bag pin) has no home: temp forgets at boot, personal follows the face's devices.
# ''A draft routes by its `draft.of` FIELD on SAVE; DELETE placement follows the landed ledger and layer order.'' RULED (the field drives the switch). The cascade's `[is[draft]…]` reads the tiddler the save carries; `_flushHand` takes the bag of this shore's last acknowledged write of the title first, then the landed ledger's bag, and falls back to the cascade's title read when neither knows the title. `_tombstoneBag` chooses the eligible layer by composition order; a draft's own deletion in a save, rename or cancel starts from its draft-book bag (`_actBody`), and `_tombstoneBag` chooses the layer. Witness: `tests/lar-kind.test.ts`.
# ''A non-meme file enters by three doors and leaves by one, and foreign titles leave by none.'' Enter: (a) `lares ingest --source --to` scans `.mem` and any extension, pairs a `.meta` sidecar, derives the URI by the address siting rule (`ingest-core.ts:83-88`, `:111-113`, `:171-181`); the island runs `tw5.parseFields(meta)` then `tw5.deserialize(ext, text, base)` (`action-handler.ts:863-873`) and packs foreign-titled members into `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (`:815-833`). (b) `act LOAD --to` takes carriers with the verb, same registry route (`:641-707`). (c) the in-wiki drag-drop / `$:/Import` ride TW5's own DOM deserializer and then the cascade — no house code touches it. Leave: the ONE render shore `exportCarrierFile` (`meme-write.ts:40-77`) → `makeTw5FileInfo` (`tw5-file-info.ts:88-176`) picks `.tid` / content + `.meta` / `.json` exactly as `generateTiddlerFileInfo` does, base64 for a binary type (`:140`), and the projector sites it at `<uri-path><ext>` (`disk-projector.ts` `flush`). But `carrierBaseRelPath` sites only `lar:///w.w.w/…` names (`bag-paths.ts:84-99`): a `.png` ingested under a `lar:` URI round-trips; a `HelloThere.tid` pack member reaches disk only through REPACK of its pack (`action-handler.ts:352-370`).
# ''The meme read over a recipe (`get mu=assert recipe=<slug>`) reads the designated bag, not the stack'' — DISSOLVED by ruling ("The stack."). GET walks the whole cascade top-down and answers from the first bag holding a record under the root, where a tombstone answers the meme absent; PUT writes the designated bag alone. Witness: `tests/meme-verbs.test.ts` "READS THE STACK"; two-vessel e2e ⑦ ★ (canon answers through `--recipe` on B).
# ''Two recipe shapes, one name'' — DISSOLVED. `recipeRecordFields` ⇆ `recipeFromRecord` (`@lararium/mesh` wiki-recipe.ts); `catalog` leaves the user stack; the live lares bag mounts as a library like the lararium bag (a record that names it mounts it), and the system recipes alone name either: every other wiki reads both through the floor's snapshots. The libraries a record names lay at boot AND reconcile live.
# ''`working` and `personal` against the four strata'' — RULED. "named wiki bag" = `working`; `personal` keeps its own layer. The daemon wiki also mounts a working layer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/questions`>>

!! Questions the operator answered, and the one still open

# ''Does a draft fleet-sync, or stay on the device?'' RULED: fleet when a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap stands, else the device floor; the cap-stack falls to the floor, never reds.
# ''Does `personal` survive as a layer?'' RULED: its own layer, while the browser UX stands up.
# ''Which per-device state MUST survive a reboot?'' OPEN. Temp forgets; personal follows the fleet; the draft floor of an unseated vessel stands as the one per-device CRDT doc.
# ''Does "named wiki bag" mean `working`?'' RULED by the disk sentence: `working`; the shore-law MOVE stays the promotion door.
# ''Does the meme read over a recipe (`get mu=assert recipe=<slug>`) read the stack?'' RULED: "The stack."
# ''Does the `draft.of` FIELD decide routing?'' RULED: `draft.of` drives draft routing; DELETE placement follows the landed ledger and layer order.
# ''Which non-meme file types enter through `lares ingest`?'' Every extension, through TW5's registry; binaries under `bags/` read OPEN (talk-story).
# ''Does the daemon wiki gain its `working` layer?'' RULED: working layers for all wikis; the late attach stands.
# ''Do the route skins and the in-VM face ship as one bundle, or two?'' RULED: ''one bundle, the caps decide what rings''. The ruling, its three grounds and what it leaves open stand at api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/one-bundle.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/aftermath`>>

!! Aftermath ~ the blast-radius spiral (operator-approved)

The spiral walked every carrier the #/as-written table names and evergreened the ones whose text described retired code: `wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law` (drafts → `@draft`, volatile → `@temp`, title-read), `save-path` SP-3/SP-4 (the cascade rule; the envelope law, no `bag` field routes), `disk-projection#/projection-routing` (the siting requirement for rule 2; rule 3 marked OWED), `residency-model#/yang-yin-chao` (temp outside the keyed set), `bag-wiki-uri-split` meta (`standing`, half-enactment named). The `lares-history` tree stays untouched (history, never canon).

''Tensions the first spiral surfaced, and how they closed:'' `wiki-layer-ontology#/naming-law` — re-trued to carve the draft FLOOR out (a per-DID device doc, a registry entry, never an instance mount of a group); `personal-slot#/scoping-mechanism` — the seat decides (binding when seated, floor when not); the four strata against five slots — ruled (`working` is the named wiki bag, `personal` stays); the `draft.of` field — ruled (the switch, with the delete map); the default writable = temp — cured red-first. What remains stands under api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/one-model "What remains".

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed ~ what stays open beside the model, and the readings behind it

!!! The recipe record (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/as-routed)

The catalog registry never rides a bag-stack (access ≠ load). `CompositeStore.getRecipe` / `putViaRecipe` / `buildLayersFromRecipe` and the camelCase `RecipeTiddler` are retired.

!!! What remains of the one model (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/one-model)

''What remains'' (owed, named):

* ''A stale catalog entry for house canon.'' No mount files an entry for a house-canon bag: a wiki standing on one mounts the Kahu realm's standing document where the vessel holds it, and where it holds none `mountWikiSlot` mints no document, lays no canon layer, and keys the slot bindings on the bag's floor address (`floorCanonAddress`). One resolver (`resolveHouseCanon`) answers every door, the realm's standing document first (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/offering`>> #/the-canon-offer). A vessel that booted under the earlier mount may still hold a `bags/lares` entry in its catalog; it answers no door where the realm names a document, and it still answers where the realm names none. Burning that entry stays owed.
* ''Disk legs for non-meme files:'' the siting cascades ride (api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/tw5-surfaces); binaries under `bags/` read OPEN (talk-story).

!!! The non-meme round trip, measured (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/tw5-surfaces)

''The non-meme round trip, measured'' (`tests/e2e/nonmeme-parity.test.ts`, both doors real): `note.md` + `.meta` — bytes identical, fields identical; `pack.json` — both doors keep the membership in `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (the server only under `retain-original-tiddler-path`), and the server's `--savewikifolder` explodes the pack into per-member `.tid` files where the island keeps it packed (REPACK) — named, on purpose. Two strays: (1) the island seeds the `.meta` BEFORE the deserialize (`action-handler.ts:870-873`) where TW5 merges it AFTER (`boot.js:1961`), so `type: text/markdown` in a sidecar lands as `text/x-markdown` on the island — a red held in the witness, owed to `action-handler.ts`; (2) `$origin-bag` reached the sidecar — cured in `tw5-file-info.ts` (`UNPERSISTED_FIELDS`). MEASURED, OPEN: a `.png` under bags/ enters the island as a skinny handle `photo.tid` on the `cid/` tier and the `.png` sweeps; the server keeps `photo.png` + `.meta` whole.

!!! The bridge's Road A against the bundle (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/one-bundle)

Road A of the bridge would have added a packed module to that same bundle, applying //the same law to the daemon island and the wiki island alike (one plugin)// (`outbound-bridge.mem` `#/back-parity`) — the ruling holds either road, because it rules the artifact count rather than the wire.

!!! The ask and the reading behind the two recipes (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/daemon-and-domain)

''The operator's ask, verbatim (quote license, 2026-11-14):''

> "since we use the recipe/bags model and not a single invariant-store for each Wiki (I mean, that exist above the CRDT bags 'recipe') then we have to use the `kapae` shadow-tombstone pattern sometimes when 'deleting' (imagine a recipe with the same tiddler in 3 bags, but the user decided to 'Delete' the top -> ??? vs 'kapae(shadows the underneath as also-deleted)/delete(reveals the underneath)'. Do we have a meme or ahu that clearly describes the 'recipe' differences between Daemon Wikis and Domain Wikis? Find a pono place, and write that."

''Register: Model-Standing, measured 2026-11-14.'' Before this slot no one carrier set the two recipes side by side: api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/as-mounted lays the island, daemon and host composites by MOUNT, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm`>> #/the-workbench rules the carry law by CAP CONTRACT, and <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage`>> #/the-recipe tells the daemon stack by ORGAN. This slot reads all three against the code, a row per layer, top row winning a read.

!!! The daemon's device slots (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/daemon-and-domain)

''The status door, walked on a scratch hearth (2026-11-14):'' `temp` read unwritable through `wiki_status`, its `why` reading `bag not registered`. ''OWED'': whether the daemon's `draft` and `personal` device slots project to disk, seed or travel in an export stands unmeasured.

!!! Two further classes, specified (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/daemon-and-domain)

!!! Two further classes ~ specified, OWED

No code holds either class today: no bag meta reads a `derived` key, and no door answers `derived-library-read-only`. <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/first-three-wave-map#/the-wikis-in-scope`>> defines both; this slot seats them beside the two that stand.

* ''THE DERIVED LIBRARY'' (road `L40`, `L40b`; OWED). A bag whose records ONE named tool writes as a pure function of ONE named commit of a tracked tree; its first instance, `codemap`, composes into the `lararium` recipe. Its `meta.mem` declares `cap-tier = "public"`, `home = "hearth"` and a new bag-meta key `derived = "<tool>"`, and each record carries the commit it derives from (`head`). It composes only in the ''libraries'' row, beneath the host wiki's canon, under a namespace that canon never writes (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/`), so it shadows nothing. No hand door writes it: the put (a family's text or one record), a residency `MOVE` or `COPY` naming it, a kāpae and a lift each refuse `derived-library-read-only`. One road writes it, an INGEST wave whose source root the vessel grants to that bag alone (`<LAR_ROOT>/cache/<bag>/<head>/`); a wave replaces the whole bag, and a title the new wave drops retracts to absent (a reveal, api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/delete-reveals-or-shadows, since nothing lies beneath its namespace). It never bakes into genesis, never rides a release cut, never takes an offer or a promotion, and never travels in an export or a carry; each of those doors refuses or skips by `derived`. After a re-founding it returns from its cache folder alone, by a fresh ingest. In the layer table it reads as a fourth kind of ''libraries'' row: generator-written, read-only, no mirror.
* ''THE TOPIC WIKI EVERY SEATED FACE WRITES'' (road `L35`; OWED). A domain wiki that one face mints and shares with every face of the operator seated `write`; its first instance, `house`, holds the house's shared memory, and `works` stands beside it as a minted work wiki. Its recipe matches the domain column whole, and it adds a reach law alone: a face reads its own daemon wiki and every topic wiki a share entry names it in. A workbench's rest seals for its realm's roster, so every face seated `write` writes the workbench on one vessel; and until the tiddler door relays to named wikis (road `L17-2a`), its tiddlers ride the steward's daemon wiki at the same titles.

The bag meta law owes the `derived` key beside `cap-tier` and `home` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy`>>).

!!! Delete user stories (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/delete-reveals-or-shadows)

!!! User stories

* ''Gaia 2026 ~ kāpae.'' Keoni keeps a team runbook wiki at work: canon holds the approved procedures, the workbench holds the team's edits. A deprecated procedure still sits in canon until the next review. He deletes it in the workbench; every teammate's wiki reads it gone that afternoon, canon keeps it for the reviewer, and a teammate's laptop that comes back online with a stale copy does not resurrect it.
* ''Gaia 2026 ~ reveal.'' Mele drafted a rewrite of a recipe card in her `personal` layer of the family cookbook wiki, then decided Tūtū's original reads better. She deletes with `reveal`: her rewrite leaves, and Tūtū's card from the workbench shows again, untouched.
* ''Elyncia 5492 ~ kāpae.'' At the Crossroads shrine of Harrowgate, a keeper learns that a ley-line rite in the lifted stage carries a corrupted verse. On her own device she sets it aside in the daemon working layer: the shrine's figure stops reciting it to her at once, the fleet's stage keeps the verse for the elders to judge, and her shadow shows its diff until the elders withdraw the item or re-lift it whole.
* ''Elyncia 5492 ~ reveal.'' A Household shrine's young tender scrawled her own blessing over the family's copy of the harvest litany in her `personal` layer. At the festival she wants the household's words back: she reveals, her scrawl leaves, and the litany the household agreed surfaces beneath it.

!!! What the delete doors owe (from api/pono/recipe-layer-model#/delete-reveals-or-shadows)

!!! OWED

* ''The mode word on the other doors.'' The TW5 engine's delete, `delete family=true` (CLI and `tiddler_delete(family=True)`) and the in-wiki UI delete plainly over nothing beneath and raise kāpae over a lower layer, with no `mode`; only the tiddler door names `mode` and refuses `delete-mode-needed`. The meme door owes a `mode: "reveal"` with the same consequence (`retractsOf`), and the wiki UI owes a "show what lies beneath" gesture beside Delete. A draft's removal (`_flushRemoval`) and a re-split's orphan slots (the family save) still raise kāpae over nothing beneath.
* ''`delete family=true bag=<bag>` reads one stack.'' The sink knows the daemon composite's layers alone, while a bag applies in every recipe that composes it: where another registered recipe stacks the bag above a layer holding the title, a plain retract there lets that record surface in that wiki. The door holds no listing of every registered recipe to read (MEASURED, 2026-11-21); until one stands, a `--bag` delete over a shared bag trusts its own stack.
* ''A plain retract drops a racing seated writer's edit.'' A plain delete removes the record's key from the document (`delete tiddlers[title]`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/automerge-doc-store.ts`); a seated peer's concurrent edit to the same record's fields merges into a record that no longer stands, and Automerge's merge discards it, where a tombstone kept the record and its fields. A measured risk on a shared workbench with more than one seated writer; the redesign (a retract that keeps a concurrent edit, or a kāpae while a peer stands seated) stays unchosen.
* ''A stand-in that never resolves stays marked.'' `waitHandle` releases its fallback's stand-in mark only once the real document merges in (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wait-handle.ts`); a `whenReady` that rejects leaves the fallback marked for the session, so every delete above it raises a kāpae (or refuses toward a mode) until the next boot. The safe direction, and no door clears the mark in session.
* ''The stand-in mark lives on one side.'' `markStandIn` keeps its marks in a module-level `WeakSet` the vessel writes (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/automerge-doc-store.ts`); an island worker's delete doors read their own module and never see a vessel-side mark. The wrapped stores (`kahuaLayerStore`, `floorReadFace`, and a binding's own `store` in `buildIslandRecipe`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-recipe.ts`) pass no `unknown()` through, so a stand-in behind one of them reads as an empty layer.
* ''A bag outside the composite on the meme door.'' `delete family=true bag=<bag>` over a realm steward's bag, a reached bag or a wiki instance slot sees no layers beneath its sink, so it still raises kāpae there; the recipe route reads its stack and plain-deletes where it can.
* ''A lower-kāpae door for the bag cascade.'' kapae#/law asks a deliberate lower with an effect record; the tiddler door retracts a tombstone (plainly where it hides nothing, by `reveal` where it hides a lower record), and no effect record audits that retract yet.
* ''kapae#/core-cut and #/law name DELETE among the exclusion gestures (MUST raise kāpae).'' The law owes a re-true to the 2026-11-20 ruling: DELETE deletes plainly, takes a `mode` (kāpae or reveal) by name where a lower layer holds the title, and only CLEAR, DROP and EVICT stay kāpae-only.
* ''Promotion disagrees with itself over a kāpae.'' A titled `MOVE` of a tombstoned source deletes canon's record (lands a tombstone in canon); a layer `MOVE` skips tombstones. One law owes: does promoting a workbench kāpae delete canon? (An operator ruling.)
* ''No road proposes a canon delete from outside the Kahu.'' The offer carries live titles alone, so a face's kāpae over house canon stays in its workbench or its personal layer; a "propose removal" offer stays unbuilt.
* ''Case (a) under a kāpae hides a future lower arrival.'' A kāpae over a title no lower layer held still stands up when canon later gains that title, so the face never sees canon's arrival. No door raises one there now (the ruling above); the owed cases above (a draft's removal, a re-split's orphan slot, a bag outside the composite) still can.
* ''A shadow goes unnamed where the view lends no layers.'' A consequence names `holds` and `shadowed` only where its view lends `layersOf` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts`); the meme door's receipt names `tombstonedIn` and no shadowed bags (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts`), so case (b) reads there as a tombstone with no list of what it hides.
* ''A face with no writer's seat.'' `delete family=true recipe=<slug>` lands in the record's designated bag (the working slot), which such a face mounts read-only; whether the delete refuses or lands in its `personal` layer stands unwitnessed.
* ''A reveal racing a seated writer's edit'' in the workbench (a retract against a concurrent put, under Automerge's merge): unmeasured.
* ''The domain wiki through the tiddler door'' (lane 2): the door answers the anchor alone, so every row above for a domain wiki reads from the island adaptor and the meme door.
* ''Carry of a `personal` layer's kāpae'' through export and import: unmeasured.

